invariant: INV-41
file: handshake_auth.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh rsa-ifma-callers
reason: the webpki client verifies an RSA leaf's CertificateVerify under 0
  in place of the session's ch_cfg.cpu, so a session whose caller set
  CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA runs that public operation on rsa_mont64.c. The
  verdict is the same. test/webpki_auth_ifma.h requires three calls to
  rsa_ifma_public from the aws chain's flight under a value with the bit:
  the CertificateVerify and the chain's two links. Only an x86-64 object
  makes the call, so test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds bin/webpki_auth_host
  for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without
  docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    int sig_ok = verify_leaf_signature(CH_CFG_CPU(h->t->cfg), &h->leaf, signed_hash, sig, sig_len);
--- new
    int sig_ok = verify_leaf_signature(0U, &h->leaf, signed_hash, sig, sig_len);
